#
# holt — FSharp for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract FSharp symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `FSharp`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own FSharp parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"FSharp\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### F# #########################################################################
--langdef=HoltFSharp
--map-HoltFSharp=+.fs
--map-HoltFSharp=+.fsi
--map-HoltFSharp=+.fsx
--kinddef-HoltFSharp=f,function,functions
--kinddef-HoltFSharp=c,class,types and modules
--regex-HoltFSharp=/^[ \t]*let[ \t]+(rec[ \t]+)?(inline[ \t]+)?([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_']*)/\3/f/
--regex-HoltFSharp=/^[ \t]*(type|module|namespace)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_'.]*)/\2/c/
--regex-HoltFSharp=/^[ \t]*member[ \t]+(this\.|_\.)?([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_']*)/\2/f/
